            <ArticleTitle>Small Circular Rep-Encoding Single-Stranded DNA Genomes in Peruvian Diarrhea Virome.</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">e00822-17</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1128/genomeA.00822-17</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Metagenomic analysis of diarrhea samples revealed the presence of numerous human enteric viruses and small circular Rep-encoding single-stranded DNA (CRESS-DNA) genomes. One such genome was related to smacoviruses, while eight others were related to genomes reported in the feces of different mammals. The tropism of these CRESS-DNA viruses remains unknown.</AbstractText>
